The tvOS simulator reports a lower GPU family than any Apple TV, so MoltenVK turns off
indirect drawing with a base instance, which Minecraft needs. The Mac GPU behind it has it.

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
index 9772757..23dd09f 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
@@ -2598,6 +2598,9 @@
 
 // iOS, tvOS and visionOS adjustments necessary when running on the simulator.
 #if MVK_OS_SIMULATOR
+	// MCTV: the tvOS simulator draws with the Mac GPU, which supports these (scripts/build-moltenvk.sh).
+	_metalFeatures.indirectDrawing = true;
+	_metalFeatures.baseVertexInstanceDrawing = true;
 	_metalFeatures.mtlBufferAlignment = 256;	// Even on Apple Silicon
 	_metalFeatures.mtlConstantBufferAlignment = 256;
 #endif
